<details class="doc-accordion"><summary><h3>Audit Rules Reviewed</h3></summary><div class="section-block">
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">No text-heavy images or flyers</div><div class="point-detail">Clear as written. A spot check: confirm and move on when it follows the rule or has no text.</div></div>
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">Linked PDFs are tagged for accessibility</div><div class="point-detail">To be rewritten once the PDF check-and-fix tool is ready.</div></div>
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">Headings are in order</div><div class="point-detail">Clear to Hot Lab regulars; needs more explanation for others. Heading sizes to be proposed.</div></div>
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">Overview page is labeled with the department name</div><div class="point-detail">Walked through with the Academics example.</div></div>
</div></details>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="g2" class="doc-group"><h2 class="eyebrow" id="g2">What We Decided</h2><p class="group-note">Decisions made in the meeting and questions still open.</p>
<details class="doc-accordion" open><summary><h3>Decisions</h3></summary><div class="section-block">
<div class="highlight-row"><div class="hl-label">Confirmed</div><div class="hl-text"><strong>No more certification extensions after Monday, November 9.</strong> Anyone not finished loses access until they complete it.</div></div>
<div class="highlight-row"><div class="hl-label">Confirmed</div><div class="hl-text"><strong>LAB credit is closed out by hand.</strong> If you have your certification badge, you are done.</div></div>
<div class="highlight-row"><div class="hl-label">Confirmed</div><div class="hl-text"><strong>The meeting after your audit is about marketing.</strong> You can schedule it once your audit is complete. The WCM attends, and the director is encouraged to attend.</div></div>
<div class="highlight-row"><div class="hl-label">Confirmed</div><div class="hl-text"><strong>Directors get one overview page.</strong> Their WCM's status, actions, analytics, Hot Lab notes and widgets in one place.</div></div>
<div class="highlight-row"><div class="hl-label">Confirmed</div><div class="hl-text"><strong>Information in an image must also be on the page as text.</strong> Alt text alone is not enough for a flyer.</div></div>
<div class="highlight-row"><div class="hl-label">Confirmed</div><div class="hl-text"><strong>The PDF rule will be rewritten around the new PDF tool.</strong></div></div>
</div></details>
<details class="doc-accordion"><summary><h3>Open Questions</h3></summary><div class="section-block">
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">Department websites within ISD</div><div class="point-detail">Whether ISD departments have their own sites is for the directors to settle first.</div></div>
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">Heading sizes</div><div class="point-detail">New sizes to be proposed and shown side by side, pending a check that they can be changed site-wide.</div></div>
</div></details>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="g3" class="doc-group"><h2 class="eyebrow" id="g3">Your To-Do List</h2><p class="group-note">Who does what next.</p>
<details class="doc-accordion" open><summary><h3>Action Items</h3></summary><div class="section-block">
<div class="action-item"><div class="action-num">1</div><div class="action-body"><div class="action-title">Finish certification</div><div class="action-detail">If you have not completed it, finish before Monday, November 9, or access comes off until you do.</div><div class="action-owner">Owner: Department WCMs not yet certified</div></div></div>
<div class="action-item"><div class="action-num">2</div><div class="action-body"><div class="action-title">Reach out to WCMs who have not finished, and close out LAB credit</div><div class="action-detail">Individually, with their directors where support is needed.</div><div class="action-owner">Owner: Sean A. Russell</div></div></div>
<div class="action-item"><div class="action-num">3</div><div class="action-body"><div class="action-title">Talk with your director about a department website</div><div class="action-detail">Your director confirms with the other directors first. Then schedule time with Sean to get started.</div><div class="action-owner">Owner: Ernesto Gonzalez</div></div></div>
<div class="action-item"><div class="action-num">4</div><div class="action-body"><div class="action-title">Propose new heading sizes</div><div class="action-detail">Side-by-side mock-ups for the District Web Team and WCMs, and a check that the change can be made site-wide.</div><div class="action-owner">Owner: Sean A. Russell</div></div></div>
<div class="action-item"><div class="action-num">5</div><div class="action-body"><div class="action-title">Build the PDF check-and-fix tool, then rewrite the PDF rule</div><div class="action-detail">The tool will also be a widget and part of the audit.</div><div class="action-owner">Owner: Sean A. Russell, with the District Web Team</div></div></div>
<div class="action-item"><div class="action-num">6</div><div class="action-body"><div class="action-title">Make audit messages say exactly what is wrong</div><div class="action-detail">From Patricia Sapp's feedback: name the image or document and what to change.</div><div class="action-owner">Owner: District Web Team</div></div></div>
<div class="action-item"><div class="action-num">7</div><div class="action-body"><div class="action-title">Keep working your audit</div><div class="action-detail">Spot-check image items and confirm the ones that are fine. Use Still stuck? on anything that does not make sense.</div><div class="action-owner">Owner: Department WCMs</div></div></div>
</div></details>
<details class="doc-accordion"><summary><h3>Next Steps</h3></summary><div class="section-block">
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">Next Hot Lab</div><div class="point-detail">Tuesday, November 10, 11:30 AM. The audit rule walkthrough continues.</div></div>
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">Coming up</div><div class="point-detail">The director overview page, the PDF tool, proposed heading sizes, and clearer audit messages.</div></div>
</div></details>
</section>
